  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed with する to form a verb. Takes に to indicate the host: ～に{寄生|きせい}する. The figurative sense (sense 2) is commonly used to criticize adults who depend entirely on their parents or others.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {寄生虫|きせいちゅう} (parasite)\n- ～に{寄生|きせい}する (to be parasitic on)\n- {寄生|きせい}{植物|しょくぶつ} (parasitic plant)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {帰省|きせい}: returning to one's hometown — a homophone with different kanji\n- {規制|きせい}: regulation — another homophone with different kanji\n- {共生|きょうせい}: symbiosis — a mutually beneficial relationship, unlike parasitism",
